    "startup": "Security environment supplied at process creation. The pinned BaseContainer implementation creates the root suspended, explicitly lists standard handles in pipe mode, assigns a kill Job before first resume and reaps failures.",
    "filesystem": "Native FS_DENY can supersede an applicable ambient grant. Same-path deny wins. A more specific explicit writable descendant can override a parent deny. Drive-root grant exception is documented for grants. Neither a complete object-scope allowlist nor coverage of future namespace changes follows from a drive list.",
    "registry": "No host-hive/key write policy is carried by the pinned PSEC schema or mapper. LPAC is rejected by this runner. Generic capability names and ordinary AppContainer/token authorization remain relevant. Separate implicit kernel or virtualization rules have not been established for this specific PSEC tree.",
    "alternative_layer": "No independent scoped Registry enforcement layer in the existing runner can gate arbitrary Windows Registry calls made directly by descendants. The trusted broker only authorizes the operations entering its own interface.",
    "inherited_authority": "Standard IO handles are allowlisted at launch. An access token or newly installed name-based path policy alone cannot be credited with revoking access on handles already held, later duplicated or passed by an authorized helper. Descendant/handle boundaries require their own verification."
  },
